Well, the amulet of life saving is completely optional for ascension,
and it's pretty easy to get your AC down so low that it doesn't matter
w/o body armor (even w/o finding a shirt).  The worse problem for me is
not being able to wear a robe.

The one I just ascended had -29 AC or so between 10 protection, +5
robe, +5 helm, +4 gloves, +4 boots, and +5 shield.

I got an early wish for the Eye of the Aethiopica, and used that for
MR.

Other options:
1. Shield of reflection -- limits spellcasting and is quite dangerous
to take off.
2. A quest artifact for MR to open up the cloak slot--best if it's
_not_ your own, since Rodney likes to steal that
3. If you get to be high level and max your luck, you can wear body
armor and still hit things fine
4. If you get all resistances and geno black dragons, you can make do
without reflection (though rings/wands in main inv may be susceptible
to explosion by lightning).
5. I suppose longbow if Diana gives reflection, but you have to wield
it so not a great option.



